 "help.hotbar_keys": "1..9 choose the hotbar slot, the wheel switches slots too.",
 "help.rebind_hint": "Every key can be changed: pause menu -> Settings -> Keys.",
 "help.quests_progress": "Done: {done} of {total}",
 "help.quests_hint": "The chain is a hint, not a rule: play however you like. The settings screen can start it over.",
 "help.world_biomes.title": "Biomes",
 "help.world_biomes.text": "The land is split into biomes: meadow, forest, desert, snowy tundra,\nswamp and caves. Trees grow best in a forest, ore hides in caves,\nanimals prefer meadows. A swamp and a tundra are slow to cross.",
 "help.world_seasons.title": "Seasons",
 "help.world_seasons.text": "A season lasts a few game days: spring, summer, autumn, winter.\nSpring and autumn give extra berries and mushrooms, winter slows\neverybody down and the weather turns rough. The clock is in the\ncorner of the minimap: day number and season.",
 "help.world_survival.title": "Hunger, cold and warmth",
 "help.world_survival.text": "Hunger grows all the time: eat food from the hotbar (the key for\n«the best food» is in the settings). At night and underground it is\ndark - a torch or a campfire lights the way, and a fire also keeps\nyou warm in winter.",
 "help.world_water.title": "Water and fishing",
 "help.world_water.text": "You can wade into the water, but you swim slowly; a bridge makes\na proper crossing. With a fishing rod in hand the gather key casts a\nline - a river or a lake is worth stopping at.",
 "help.civ_city.title": "Your city",
 "help.civ_city.text": "Build a town center to found a city, then a country (in the cities\nscreen). A city lives on taxes: part of what its people gather goes\ninto the city storage and pays for shared buildings.",
 "help.civ_roles.title": "Roles and rights",
 "help.civ_roles.text": "A leader names elders, builders, warriors and citizens. A right decides\nwho may build, fight or spend the city fund.",
 "help.civ_taxes.title": "Taxes and the fund",
 "help.civ_taxes.text": "The leader sets the tax (0-40 %). The fund holds wood, stone and food\nfor the city walls, the market and the wonder.",
 "help.civ_war.title": "War and victory",
 "help.civ_war.text": "A country may declare war, besiege a city and take it; the towers and\nthe walls slow the attackers down. A game is won by the country that\ntakes every other city or finishes the wonder.",
